course: dictionary
lesson: 14150
title: Spotting a misprint
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A misprint is a mistake in something that has been printed, like a wrong letter, word or number. Printed things can be books, newspapers, menus or timetables. «The menu said soup costs 5 pounds, but it was a misprint and should have said 3 pounds.»
explain: You can often spot a misprint by using the clues around it. If a sentence does not make sense, or a number looks wrong, check it. «The bus leaves at 9 pm for school.» School buses do not leave at night, so pm must be a misprint for am.
explain: In maths, a misprint in a question can make it impossible to solve. If you think a question has a misprint, tell your teacher. Do not guess the answer to a question that is broken.
fact: A misprint is a mistake made when something is printed.
fact: Misprints can happen in newspapers, books, menus and timetables.
fact: «It must be a misprint» means the mistake was made when the words or numbers were printed.
fact: To misprint means to print something wrongly, as in «The printer misprinted the date».
fact: In maths, a misprint can make a question impossible to solve, so tell the teacher.
exercise: «The sign said the shop opens at 9 pm, but it was a misprint.» What is a misprint? | A sweet treat from the bakery | *A mistake in something printed | A loud noise from the street | A picture that has faded
exercise: «The book had a misprint: "the cat sat on the mat" was spelled "teh cat sat on teh mat".» Which word is the misprint? | *teh | mat | cat | sat
exercise: Ella says, «The timetable says maths is at 4 o'clock, but I have never had maths at night. It must be a misprint.» What does Ella mean? | The bell is broken | Maths has moved to a new room | The timetable was drawn by hand | *The timetable has a printed mistake
test: «The menu said a burger costs 50 pounds, but it was a misprint for 5 pounds.» What does misprint mean in this sentence? | A message from the chef | A new kind of burger | *A printed mistake | A drink with no sugar
test: To misprint means to print something wrongly. Which sentence uses misprint as a verb? | The misprint was on page four | *The newspaper misprinted the football score, and the team lost in print | The newspaper misprinted the football score | I read a book about cats
exam: «The question said 7 plus 5 equals 20, which is a misprint.» Why might a misprint in a maths question matter? | It can make the question impossible to solve, so tell the teacher | *It makes the question easier to solve | It means the answer is always 20 | It shows the printer was happy
